# n8n: Receipt-to-warranty tracker

Send a photo of a receipt to a Telegram bot. The receipt is read by a local vision model, logged in a Notion database with the image attached, and a daily check reminds me before a warranty or return window runs out.

Built to track big purchases without typing anything in: take a photo, get a confirmation message, done.

## How it works

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  subgraph IN["Capture"]
    A["Receipt photo (Telegram)"] --> B["Poll Telegram every minute"]
    B --> C["Download image"]
  end
  subgraph AI["Read (local)"]
    C --> D["Ollama vision model (qwen2.5vl:7b)"]
    D --> E["Parse JSON, work out coverage"]
  end
  subgraph OUT["Log"]
    E --> F["Create Notion row"]
    F --> G["Upload receipt image to the row"]
    G --> H["Telegram confirmation"]
  end
  subgraph REM["Reminders"]
    R1["Daily 8am"] --> R2["Query Notion: coverage ending in 30 days"]
    R2 --> R3["Telegram reminder"]
  end
```

## Coverage rule

The model is asked to return only what is printed on the receipt. No warranty is ever assumed.

| Receipt says | Coverage Type | Coverage End |
|---|---|---|
| A warranty period | Warranty | Purchase date + warranty months |
| No warranty, but a return window | Return window | Purchase date + return days |
| Neither | None | Left blank |

## Notion database

The workflow writes to a Warranties database with these properties.

| Property | Type | Filled by |
|---|---|---|
| Item | Title | Model |
| Retailer | Text | Model |
| Amount | Number | Model |
| Purchase Date | Date | Model |
| Product Model/Serial | Text | Model (model or serial number if printed) |
| Warranty Length (months) | Number | Model, only when a warranty is printed |
| Coverage Type | Select: Warranty, Return window, None | Workflow |
| Coverage End | Date | Workflow |
| Status | Select: Active, Expired, Claimed | Workflow sets Active when there is coverage |
| Receipt Image | Files | Workflow (Notion file upload API) |

## Setup

1. Pull a vision-capable model in Ollama, for example `ollama pull qwen2.5vl:7b`.
2. Create a dedicated Telegram bot with @BotFather and copy its token.
3. Create a Notion internal integration and share the Warranties database with it.
4. In n8n, import [`receipt-warranty-tracker.json`](receipt-warranty-tracker.json).
5. Fill in the placeholders:
   - `PASTE_YOUR_BOT_TOKEN_HERE` in the **Poll Telegram** node
   - `YOUR_NOTION_DATABASE_ID` in **Parse and Calculate Warranty** and **Find Expiring Warranties**
   - `YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` in **Send Reminder**
   - the Ollama URL in **Ollama Reads Receipt** (`host.docker.internal` works when n8n runs in Docker on the same machine as Ollama)
6. Select your Telegram and Notion credentials on the nodes that show a warning.
7. Send a receipt photo, run the workflow once to test, then publish it so the schedule runs on its own.

No secrets are stored in the export. All credentials are placeholders.

## Design decisions

- **Local model.** Receipts are read by Ollama on the Nebula PC, so purchase data stays on my own network and there is no per-receipt cost. The trade-off is lower accuracy than a hosted model, so the confirmation message repeats what was logged.
- **Polling instead of a webhook.** n8n runs on localhost, and Telegram only sends webhooks to public HTTPS URLs. Polling every minute avoids exposing n8n at the cost of up to a minute of delay. It uses its own bot because a bot with a webhook set cannot be polled.
- **No assumed warranty.** An early version defaulted to 12 months. That was removed so the database only holds coverage that is actually stated.
- **Coverage End is calculated in n8n.** Warranties are measured in months and return windows in days, so one calculated date column keeps the reminder query simple.
- **Notion through the HTTP node.** Building the request body in code lets the workflow leave out empty properties instead of failing on blank values, and the Notion file upload API needs a three-step call (create upload, send file, attach to the row).

## Limitations

- One item per receipt: the highest-priced item is logged.
- Images only. PDF receipts are not read, and uploads are labelled as JPEG.
- Only what is printed on the receipt counts. It does not look up a retailer's return policy.
- Accuracy depends on the photo. Clear, flat, well-lit receipts work best.

## Files

- [`receipt-warranty-tracker.json`](receipt-warranty-tracker.json): the n8n workflow export
